{"total_count":867,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commits/a04abe9b91cca2a2275a46fe5277a863d721e611","sha":"a04abe9b91cca2a2275a46fe5277a863d721e611","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MzY1Njk3NDkzOmEwNGFiZTliOTFjY2EyYTIyNzVhNDZmZTUyNzdhODYzZDcyMWU2MTE=","html_url":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commit/a04abe9b91cca2a2275a46fe5277a863d721e611","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commits/a04abe9b91cca2a2275a46fe5277a863d721e611/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/commits/a04abe9b91cca2a2275a46fe5277a863d721e611","author":{"date":"2025-02-09T15:10:25.000Z","name":"Anne Baanen","email":"vierkantor@vierkantor.com"},"committer":{"date":"2025-02-09T15:10:25.000Z","name":"Anne Baanen","email":"vierkantor@vierkantor.com"},"message":"refactor(CategoryTheory/Sites,Topology/Sheaves): upgrade `HasForget` to `ConcreteCategory` (#21575)\n\nThis PR goes through all the files in `CategoryTheory/Sites` and `Topology/Sheaves` and replaces `HasForget` with `ConcreteCategory` so that we don't need to worry about `HasForget.instFunLike` or `HasForget.hasCoeToSort` mismatching with the actual coercions to functions/types.\r\n\r\nSome sources of friction remain:\r\n\r\n`Type` is not (globally) a `ConcreteCategory`, since to make it so needs to break the assumption that `forget Type` is reducibly defeq to the identity functor. The solution of this PR is to copy instances such as `PreservesLimits (forget Type)` over from the identity functor, and enabling the `ConcreteCategory` instance locally (see `CategoryTheory/Limits/ConcreteCategory/Basic.lean`). In the longer term I think we can enable that instance globally, but it would require quite some more downstream fixes.\r\n\r\nLimits are still based on `HasForget`, so we have to insert some `show` and `rfl` to change the goal from one spelling to another. Similarly for `elementwise`-generated lemmas. This should go away once we update the rest of the files to the same standards.\r\n\r\nDespite those uglifications mentioned above, I think the overall result is a clear improvement.","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/trees/637afa0de4b3b91d25189cc4290ad590141bbc79","sha":"637afa0de4b3b91d25189cc4290ad590141bbc79"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"Vierkantor","id":2116570,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTY1NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2116570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor","html_url":"https://github.com/Vierkantor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Vierkantor","id":2116570,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTY1NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2116570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor","html_url":"https://github.com/Vierkantor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vierkantor/subscriptions